    "instructions": [
      "Rinse the dry white long-grain rice under cold water until the water runs clear, then drain.",
      "In a small pot, combine the rinsed rice, water, and 1 gram of the table salt. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat, then cover with a tight-fitting lid, reduce the heat to low, and simmer for 15 minutes. Remove from heat and let sit covered for 5 minutes before fluffing with a fork.",
      "While the rice cooks, mince the raw garlic clove and cut the raw boneless skinless chicken breast into bite-sized pieces.",
      "Season the chicken evenly with the remaining 2 grams of table salt and the ground black pepper.",
      "Heat 10 grams of olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the chicken pieces and cook for 6 to 8 minutes, turning occasionally, until golden brown and cooked through to an internal temperature of 74\u00b0C (165\u00b0F). Transfer the chicken to a plate.",
      "Add the remaining 10 grams of olive oil and the minced garlic to the same skillet, cooking for 30 seconds until fragrant.",
      "Add the raw broccoli florets along with 30 grams of water (not listed in base ingredients, for steam). Cover immediately with a lid to steam for 4 to 5 minutes until crisp-tender and vibrant green.",
      "Return the cooked chicken to the skillet with the broccoli, tossing everything together for 1 minute to reheat and combine flavors.",
      "Divide the warm rice, chicken, and broccoli evenly between two plates and serve immediately."
